WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.395
Your pipeline works on your laptop.

2
00:00:02.415 --> 00:00:03.705
Good start.

3
00:00:03.725 --> 00:00:08.390
Now it must run every night, retry on its own, and alert you when it is stuck.

4
00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:13.240
Two ideas: who conducts the work, and how you ship changes safely.

5
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.352
Think of an orchestra.

6
00:00:14.372 --> 00:00:16.175
Someone has to conduct.

7
00:00:16.195 --> 00:00:18.450
Cloud Composer is managed Airflow.

8
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:22.560
Pick it for big jobs with many steps, retries and backfills.

9
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.635
Workflows is light and serverless.

10
00:00:24.655 --> 00:00:27.420
Pick it for a short chain of API calls.

11
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.820
Cloud Scheduler is just an alarm clock.

12
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.330
It fires one thing, on a schedule.

13
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:36.815
And for a single SQL query each night, a scheduled query is enough.

14
00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:39.215
The trap: Composer for one nightly query.

15
00:00:39.235 --> 00:00:40.900
That is far too much.

16
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.600
One more.

17
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.350
Airflow only conducts.

18
00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:47.675
The heavy work runs in BigQuery, Dataflow or Dataproc.

19
00:00:47.695 --> 00:00:51.160
A good task can run twice, and give the same result.

20
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.272
The word for that is idempotent.

21
00:00:53.292 --> 00:00:54.960
Overwrite the day's partition.

22
00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.595
Do not append again.

23
00:00:56.615 --> 00:00:59.508
And use the run's date from Airflow, not the clock.

24
00:00:59.528 --> 00:01:02.345
Then backfills load the right day.

25
00:01:02.365 --> 00:01:05.155
Idea two: shipping changes safely.

26
00:01:05.175 --> 00:01:06.330
The rule is simple.

27
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:07.867
Everything lives in Git.

28
00:01:07.887 --> 00:01:10.290
Nobody edits production by hand.

29
00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.402
Cloud Build tests and deploys.

30
00:01:12.422 --> 00:01:14.928
Artifact Registry stores the images.

31
00:01:14.948 --> 00:01:17.425
Terraform builds the infrastructure.

32
00:01:17.445 --> 00:01:21.137
With Terraform, dev, test and prod are built the same way.

33
00:01:21.157 --> 00:01:24.200
So what works in test works in prod.

34
00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.460
Recap.

35
00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.023
Composer for big DAGs.

36
00:01:27.043 --> 00:01:28.710
Workflows for light chains.

37
00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.170
Scheduler for one thing on a clock.

38
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.020
Make tasks safe to run twice.

39
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.080
And keep everything as code.

40
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.167
Line two, done.

41
00:01:36.187 --> 00:01:38.925
Try the checkpoint below.
